      children: [(0,jsx_runtime.jsx)(_components.strong, {
        children: "Osho Darshan:"
      }), " Arjuna names the qualification of the true teacher: only one who knows can cut the knot of the doubter. Osho says this verse is about the need for a living answer — the doubt about failure is not a book-doubt; it is a heart-doubt, and only a living teacher can cut it. Krishna answers not with a doctrine but with a presence: the answer itself is an act of friendship. And there is a quieter teaching here: bring your real questions, the ones you are ashamed of, to the one who can hold them. The doubt that is spoken is already half-dissolved; the doubt that is hidden hardens."]
